# Copy to cloud/.env and fill in. cloud/.env is git-ignored by convention — never commit secrets.

# ⚠️ AUTH POLICY (confirmed by the InDesign API team, 2026-09-09):
#   Capability REGISTRATION (--register / the register step of --submit) accepts
#   ONLY a Developer Console OAuth Server-to-Server token (Path C below). An IMSS
#   service token (Path A/B) is rejected on the write path with
#   400 "Unable to get the IMS Organization" — it works for reads (--ping) only.
#   The Dev Console "InDesign API – Firefly Services" project appears only once the
#   IMS org is entitled to the Firefly Services product.

# --- Adobe IMS auth: pick ONE path ---
#
# Path C — OAuth Server-to-Server (client_credentials). ★ REQUIRED for registration. ★
#   Adobe Developer Console -> "InDesign API – Firefly Services" project ->
#   OAuth Server-to-Server credential. Use its client id + secret here, and make
#   sure FFS_AUTH_CODE is EMPTY so run.mjs uses client_credentials (not a service token).
FFS_CLIENT_ID=
FFS_CLIENT_SECRET=
#   Current InDesign guidance: request firefly_api (indesign_services kept for back-compat).
FFS_SCOPES=openid,AdobeID,firefly_api,ff_apis,indesign_services
#   Stage project -> stage IMS host; prod project -> https://ims-na1.adobelogin.com/ims/token/v3
IMS_ENDPOINT=https://ims-na1-stg1.adobelogin.com/ims/token/v1
#
# Path A — IMSS service-token client (durable). READS ONLY — cannot register.
#   Kept for --ping / --check-auth. From imss.corp.adobe.com -> client (pnam-ffs-api,
#   STAGE) -> Service Tokens -> "Permanent Authorization Code" -> Show. Exchanged per
#   run (grant_type=authorization_code, scope=system — the API scopes ride from the
#   client config). LEAVE EMPTY when you want Path C to run.
FFS_AUTH_CODE=
#
# Path B — ephemeral bearer token (quick read test only; expires ~8h). Overrides A/C.
#   IMSS -> Service Tokens -> "Generate short-lived service token".
FFS_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# IMS Organization ID (…@AdobeOrg) — REQUIRED by the InDesign API as the
# x-gw-ims-org-id header (it can't resolve org from a service token alone).
FFS_ORG_ID=

# --- optional overrides (defaults live in run.mjs) ---
# InDesign host. Match it to the token's env: stage token → stage host, prod → prod.
# INDESIGN_API_BASE=https://indesign-stage.adobe.io    # prod = https://indesign.adobe.io
# INDESIGN_REGISTER_PATH=/v3/capability   # verified capability-register endpoint
# CAPABILITY_NAME=idapi-banner-exporter   # name in the bundle manifest
# INDESIGN_EXECUTE_URL=                    # paste the `url` that --register returns; used by --submit
# STORAGE_MODE=unset          # unset | adobe | s3 | azure  (see README → Storage)
# POLL_INTERVAL_MS=4000
# POLL_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
